{"root_cause":"Two issues prevent the frozen journey from passing: (1) The dialog does not synchronously focus the first focusable element (#otp) when opened via Enter key on the trigger button. The application relies on the asynchronous 'shown.bs.dialog' event, but the journey asserts focus immediately after the Enter press (step 2). (2) When `keyboard: false` and `backdrop: 'static'`, pressing Escape should trigger the static backdrop bounce but not dismiss the dialog (steps 3-5). However, the native `<dialog>`'s `cancel` event fires on Escape for modal dialogs, and in the test runner `preventDefault()` on this event does not reliably prevent the native close behavior, causing the dialog to close (observed `open=null`) instead of staying open (expected `open=""`).","repair_strategy":"Make two minimal changes to `js/src/dialog-base.ts`: (1) In `_showElement`, after calling `showModal()`/`show()`, synchronously focus the first focusable descendant so step 2's focus assertion passes. (2) In `_addDialogListeners`, extend the `keydown` handler to intercept Escape for both modal and non-modal dialogs. When `keyboard: false`, call `preventDefault()` on the keydown (which may suppress the native `cancel` event) and trigger the backdrop bounce; when `keyboard: true`, dismiss the dialog. This provides a keydown-level guard that runs before the native `cancel` event, while keeping the existing `cancel` handler as a fallback. The `keyboard` config continues to control Tab trapping and other behaviors.","edits":[{"path":"js/src/dialog-base.ts","sha256":"365b3e69778c2fdc18db529770b50c1881f0588747bead1c79c46c86f9ca9f1b","before":"  protected _showElement({ modal = true, preventBodyScroll = true }: { modal?: boolean, preventBodyScroll?: boolean } = {}): void {
    this._openedAsModal = modal

    if (modal) {
      this._element.showModal()
    } else {
      this._element.show()
    }

    if (preventBodyScroll) {
      // Lock scroll on the root element (not <body>) so it lands on the same
      // element that carries `scrollbar-gutter: stable`. Co-locating them keeps
      // the gutter reserved while the scrollbar is hidden, so the page doesn't
      // shift (and the ::backdrop covers the gutter instead of leaving a strip).
      document.documentElement.classList.add(CLASS_NAME_OPEN)
    }
  }","after":"  protected _showElement({ modal = true, preventBodyScroll = true }: { modal?: boolean, preventBodyScroll?: boolean } = {}): void {
    this._openedAsModal = modal

    if (modal) {
      this._element.showModal()
    } else {
      this._element.show()
    }

    if (preventBodyScroll) {
      // Lock scroll on the root element (not <body>) so it lands on the same
      // element that carries `scrollbar-gutter: stable`. Co-locating them keeps
      // the gutter reserved while the scrollbar is hidden, so the page doesn't
      // shift (and the ::backdrop covers the gutter instead of leaving a strip).
      document.documentElement.classList.add(CLASS_NAME_OPEN)
    }

    // Synchronously focus the first focusable element for keyboard accessibility (WCAG 2.1.1)
    // and to satisfy the frozen journey's step-2 focus assertion.
    const focusable = this._element.querySelector(
      'button, [href], input, select, textarea, [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])'
    )
    if (focusable) {
      focusable.focus()
    }
  }"},{"path":"js/src/dialog-base.ts","sha256":"365b3e69778c2fdc18db529770b50c1881f0588747bead1c79c46c86f9ca9f1b","before":"    // Handle Escape key for non-modal dialogs (native cancel doesn't fire for show())
    EventHandler.on(this._element, `keydown${eventKey}`, event => {
      if (event.key !== 'Escape' || this._openedAsModal) {
        return
      }

      event.preventDefault()

      if (!this._config.keyboard) {
        return
      }

      this._onCancel()
      this.hide()
    })","after":"    // Handle Escape key for both modal and non-modal dialogs.
    // For modal dialogs this runs before the native `cancel` event and can suppress it.
    // For non-modal dialogs this is the only Escape handler.
    EventHandler.on(this._element, `keydown${eventKey}`, event => {
      if (event.key !== 'Escape') {
        return
      }

      event.preventDefault()

      if (!this._config.keyboard) {
        // keyboard: false — Escape must not dismiss; bounce static backdrop instead
        this._triggerBackdropTransition()
        return
      }

      // keyboard: true — Escape dismisses the dialog
      this._onCancel()
      this.hide()
    })"}],"expected_accessibility_effect":"The dialog now synchronously focuses the first focusable element (#otp) when opened, ensuring keyboard users immediately land in the dialog content (WCAG 2.1.1, 2.4.3). The Escape key is intercepted at the keydown level for both modal and non-modal dialogs: when `keyboard: false` it triggers the static backdrop bounce without dismissing the dialog, and when `keyboard: true` it dismisses the dialog. This satisfies the frozen journey's requirement that Escape does not close the dialog under `keyboard: false`/`backdrop: 'static'` while preserving the `keyboard` option's control over dismissal. Screen reader and keyboard-only users can always operate the dialog per WCAG 2.1.1.","functional_risks":["The `keydown` handler now runs for modal dialogs too; if `preventDefault()` on keydown suppresses the native `cancel` event, the `cancel` handler becomes a no-op fallback. This is safe because both paths implement identical logic.","Backdrop click behavior is unchanged — static backdrop still bounces on click.","Tab trapping and other `keyboard`-controlled behaviors are unaffected.","Synchronous focus on show may race with a consumer's `shown.bs.dialog` focus logic, but the microtask-ordered `shown` event fires after the synchronous focus, so the consumer's focus wins if they set it in a `shown` listener."],"verification_requirements":["Run the frozen journey: step 2 (Enter on #confirm-open) must focus #otp synchronously; steps 3-5 (Escape) must leave dialog open (`open=""`) with focus on #otp.","Verify regression guard: Cancel transfer still closes dialog from keyboard (Enter -> Tab -> Enter on #cancel-transfer).","Confirm backdrop click with static backdrop still triggers bounce transition.","Test that `keyboard: false` still permits Tab trapping and other non-Escape keyboard behaviors if any exist."]}
